# The raw M5 download is never committed: it is ~500 MB and scripts/download_data.py
# fetches it. The one exception is data/sample_panel.parquet, the 300 sampled series
# trimmed to 842 days (~300 KB), which is committed so that a fresh clone can run the app,
# the tests and scripts/analyse.py without the download. Licence and attribution for it
# live in data/README.md.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
!data/README.md
!data/sample_panel.parquet

# Results are regenerated by scripts/run_ladder.py and scripts/analyse.py. Two committed
# exceptions, both small and both load-bearing:
#   results/raw/         the forecasts every rung produced (~4.5 MB). Committing them is
#                        what makes the analysis reproducible without two hours of compute,
#                        and what lets the app re-cost the business case live.
#   results/published/   the summary tables and figures the README and case study cite.
results/*
!results/.gitkeep
!results/published/
!results/raw/

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
lightning_logs/
*.ckpt
.DS_Store
